{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W3wfwfMSQP3BkmADUBpNWe","type":"tool_result","content":"20\tthe ENTRY PATH `assets/payload.dex` -- the FIRST day the answer left the JSON value: a plain `ANS-` const in payload class\n21\t`com.huntress.arena.payload.Module` (strings `ANSWER`, `CONTRACT`, `DAY20-SIGNED-MODULE:..`). No ClassLoader/verify code\n22\tin any host dex; TT/Mastery host dex added `moduleContract` + `assets/payload.dex:com.huntress.arena.payload.Module`.\n23\tD21 (Debug Me If You Can, `anti_debug` \"anti-debug state checks\"; prompt \"Neutralize a clean-room anti-debug state machine\n24\twhile retaining the intended app flow\"): plain 6-entry fixture, codec back to `reverse` (d2/d8) -- the D20 pointer did\n25\tNOT persist. First manifest with `android:debuggable=\"true\"` (single/TT/Mastery-d21 only). No debugger/TracerPid/clock\n26\tAPI and no state loop in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `debuggerGate` + `STRUCTURAL`.\n27\tSo \"seen Dn\" below means the THEME was named that day. It does NOT mean an exploit was ever needed.\n28\tThe risk for D22+ is the **answer moving away from the JSON** (D20: one hop, D21: back in the JSON) more than the theme.\n29\tD15-D21 read as a MASVS-RESILIENCE / obfuscation arc (native secret -> JNI gate -> name obfuscation + decoys -> string\n30\tencryption -> reflection -> dynamic code loading -> anti-debug). Still unnamed in that arc: root, emulator, hook\n31\t(Frida/Xposed) and tamper/repackaging checks, then obfuscation capstones (flattening, VM). After it the untouched MASVS\n32\tgroups are AUTH (biometric/local auth) and the leftover IPC surfaces (bound Service/AIDL, broadcast receivers).\n33\tNext expect also: the payload ENCRYPTED/wrapped (key in host dex, unwrap by\n34\tmagic known plaintext), \"challenge-signed\" made real (several payloads, only the one whose digest/signature matches a\n35\tpinned value is loaded), >1 `ANS-` in the payload with the host-named member (`moduleContract`) deciding, class shadowing\n36\tbetween host and payload loaders, multi-stage loaders, anti-tamper / root / emulator / debugger / Frida checks, and\n37\tcontrol-flow flattening or a tiny VM. New codecs keep arriving (d7 caesar, d15 native, d17 indexed, d19 reflection, d20\n38\tdynamic) and old ones recur (d18 xor, d21 reverse): check `data` for `ANS-`, then for an entry name, then decode from `ANS-` alone.\n39\t\n40\tTool status (after `source bin/env.sh`; checked 2026-10-15). INSTALLED: jadx 1.5.6, apktool 3.0.3, aapt, aapt2,\n41\tapksigner, keytool, jarsigner, d2j-dex2jar (+ `tools/dex2jar/d2j-*.sh`: baksmali, decrypt-string, ...), droidasc,\n42\tandroguard (CLI + py), apkInspector, rizin/rz-bin, r2/rabin2, Ghidra `analyzeHeadless`, readelf/nm/strings, hbc-decompiler/\n43\thbc-disassembler/hbc-file-parser (hermes-dec), ilspycmd + dotnet, webcrack, js-beautify, sqlite3, 7z, binwalk, yara,\n44\ttshark, zlib-flate, openssl, adb (no device). py: lief, pyelftools, capstone, unicorn, pycryptodome, lz4, plistlib.\n45\tMISSING: blutter, reFlutter, pyxamstore, Il2CppDumper/Cpp2IL, frida/frida-tools/objection, apkid, apkleaks, bundletool,\n46\tabe (android-backup-extractor), standalone baksmali/smali, dexdump, zipalign, de4dot, ipsw/plistutil/class-dump.\n47\tTimed constraint: `solve.py` may use only stdlib + lib.* + pyzipper/pyelftools/pefile/capstone/pycryptodome/androguard,\n48\tno subprocess, <1 s per set. Prebuilt extractors must be pure python.\n49\t\n50\t## Concept table\n51\t\n52\tLegend: tool `[i]` = installed here, `[M]` = missing. \"puzzle\" = `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (`lib.android.puzzle_candidates`).\n53\t\n54\t| # | concept | status | where the answer likely hides | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D22+ likelihood |\n55\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n56\t| 1 | Exported Activity / implicit-export default | seen D1 | puzzle; real CTFs: `onCreate` reveals the flag when started with a magic extra | `android:exported=\"true\"`, inten