-\"\n156\t                                    data = an entry path (D20 `dynamic`: assets/payload.dex)? open THAT entry, recurse from 1.\n157\t                                    int list beside data (D17 `indexed`, D5 `split`): r[order[i]] = data[i]; else gather\n158\t   lib/<abi>/*.so                   strings -a | grep ANS- ; nm -D --defined-only ; no Java_* -> JNI_OnLoad/RegisterNatives\n159\t                                    Java_*_native*(int) + *_accepts helper (D16 gate): objdump -d it; the value it returns\n160\t                                    is the answer (D16: &arena_value = the .rodata ANS- literal; bypass len 65536)\n161\t   lib/*/libapp.so + libflutter.so  Flutter: strings libapp.so; flutter_assets/kernel_blob.bin (debug = source text)\n162\t   assets/index.android.bundle      RN: head -c8 | xxd; c61fbc03 = Hermes -> hbc-decompiler; else webcrack/js-beautify\n163\t   assemblies/*.dll|*.blob, libmonodroid.so   Xamarin: XALZ = lz4 per-dll; then ilspycmd f.dll\n164\t   libil2cpp.so + global-metadata.dat         Unity IL2CPP: strings global-metadata.dat | grep ANS- ; Managed/*.dll -> ilspycmd\n165\t   assets/www/, cordova.js, capacitor.config  hybrid JS: grep -r in assets/www\n166\t   assets/*.dex|*.jar|*.apk|*.zip|*.bin       dynamic code loading (D20: plain dex, ANS- const in `...payload.Module`):\n167\t                                    strings -a it first; no dex/PK/ELF magic -> xor/known-plaintext unwrap (key from host dex);\n168\t                                    >1 payload -> the one matching the host's pinned digest; >1 ANS- -> the member the host\n169\t                                    names (`<entry>:<class>` string, `moduleContract`), never the first regex hit\n170\t   libjiagu/libsecexe/libDexHelper.so          packer: payload is the encrypted asset; static decrypt or give up early\n171\t   res/xml/network_security_config.xml        NSC: aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/network_security_config.xml\n172\t   resources.arsc                   aapt dump --values resources x.apk | grep -iE 'ans-|secret|key|flag|token'\n173\t   *.db / shared_prefs/*.xml / *.ab sqlite3 f.db .dump ; .ab: dd bs=24 skip=1 | zlib-flate -uncompress | tar x\n174\t   res/raw/*.bks|*.p12|*.pem        keystore: password is a dex string; keytool -list -v -storepass PW\n175\t   google-services.json / firebase  key/URL itself may be the answer\n176\t   base.apk + split_config.*.apk / manifest.json / toc.pb / BundleConfig.pb   split/XAPK/APKS/AAB: unzip inner, recurse\n177\t   Payload/*.app/                   iOS: plistlib Info.plist; rz-bin -zz the Mach-O\n178\t2. Plain-anywhere scan (incl. UTF-16 the zip scan misses):\n179\t   for f in $(unzip -Z1 x.apk); do unzip -p x.apk \"$f\" | strings -a -el | grep -H --label=\"$f\" ANS-; done\n180\t   7z l x.apk vs unzip -l x.apk differ -> zip tricks (dup entry / trailing data): binwalk x.apk\n181\t3. Manifest (fast): aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml | grep -E \\\n182\t   'exported|scheme|host|autoVerify|permission|debuggable|allowBackup|usesCleartext|networkSecurity|taskAffinity|launchMode|meta-data'\n183\t   meta-data value= is a hiding spot (huntress.mechanic lives there). debuggable=true (D21) is a fact, not an answer.\n184\t4. Dex triage: strings -a classes*.dex | grep -E 'DAY-|CODEC|ANS-|^[0-9A-F]{8,16}$' then map API hits to themes:\n185\t   DexClassLoader/InMemoryDexClassLoader/moduleContract -> asset dex   SecretKeySpec/AES/Cipher -> static key decrypt\n186\t   loadLibrary/RegisterNatives -> .so                     java/util/Random/setSeed/currentTimeMillis -> regenerate RNG\n187\t   MessageDigest/PBKDF2 -> hash brute                     addJavascriptInterface/loadUrl/file:///android_asset -> assets html/js\n188\t   Binder/$Stub/Messenger/onReceive -> IPC handler        CertificatePinner/sha256/ -> pins in code or NSC\n189\t   su/magisk/goldfish/frida/TracerPid/isDebuggerConnected/debuggerGate (D21) -> clean_device_scan: clean-path value\n190\t   Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod -> reflection_scan     BuildConfig / R$string -> arsc / BuildConfig.java\n191\t   Proxy/MethodHandles/invoke-custom -> real target; packed-switch in a loop / $SwitchMap$ -> flattened_cfg_scan\n192\t   KeyStore.getInstance(\"BKS\"|\"PKCS12\") -> res/raw keystore + password string\n193\t5. Read code only after 1-4: droidasc findrefs x.apk string <hit>; droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>; jadx -d w/jadx x.apk\n194\t   (add --deobf for 1-2 letter class names). Strings split across constants: rebuild order from the method body.\n195\t   String decryptors (D18 TT `EncryptedStrings.decryptByte`): dex_eval_scan, else jadx the helper, take the ARGS from\n196\t   each call site, re-implement in py; unknown key/rolling scheme -> solve it from the ANS- known plaintext.\n197\t   R8/decoys (D17): hint strings like \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\" name the chain; >1 ANS- candidate -> keep\n198\t   the one appended before `proof=` in ChallengeActivity, never the first regex hit. Reflection/dispatch (D19 theme):\n199\t   names may be encoded or picked by a key from the deep link/asset; evaluate only the invoked target, not its twins.\n200\t   lib scanners for code-side answers (not in extract_answer): renamed_chain_scan, proof_flow_scan, dex_eval_scan,\n201\t   reflection_scan, mapping_restore_scan, signing_block_scan, zip_structure_scan  (all lib.android, take apk path)\n202\t6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n203\t7. Validate: candidate must fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). Two sources (asset + .so) agreeing = submit.\n204\t8. Mastery: each set can be a different day's fixture; decode every APK on its own; loop over all answer_ids (3 or 5).\n205\t```\n206\t\n207\t## Readiness gaps\n208\t\n209\tPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n210\t`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\n211\tutf16-string-pool-scan, nested-container-recurse, dex-native-split-assembly, static-key-cipher-decode,\n212\tdecode-any-chain-peel, native-so-emulate-export, dex-string-decrypt-arrays, asset-db-prefs-backup,\n213\tidentity-derived-key, hermes-hbc-string-table, cert-and-signing-facts, il2cpp-metadata-literals,\n214\tjni-export-return-trace, jni-gate-bypass-input, registernatives-table, native-stack-string, multi-abi-arm-native,\n215\tdex-native-call-args, native-gated-branch-read, dex-gated-branch-consts, webview-asset-js-scan,\n216\tcert-pin-and-nsc-facts, puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields, proof-flow-candidate-ranking, r8-renamed-chain-follow,\n217\tdalvik-mini-interpreter, permutation-transposition-family, reflection-name-resolve, proguard-mapping-restore,\n218\tapk-signing-block-payload, zip-structure-anomaly-scan, integrity-derived-key, ans-prefix-numeric-compose,\n219\tcustom-alphabet-decode, asset-cipher-dex-loader, native-init-array-decrypt, resource-id-const-resolve,\n220\tmessagedigest-derived-answer, v1-manifest-digest-verify, dex-slack-and-header-anomaly, aab-proto-manifest-parse,\n221\trolling-xor-keystream-family, decrypt-call-site-args-eval, known-string-obfuscator-signatures,\n222\tidentifier-collision-resolve, opaque-predicate-dead-branch, java-serialized-object-parse, jwt-token-decode-verify,\n223\tprotobuf-asset-wire-decode, sqlcipher-asset-decrypt, dispatch-key-resolve, entry-reachable-callgraph-rank,\n224\tflattened-cfg-switch-eval, proxy-methodhandle-invokecustom, clean-device-env-stubs, tiny-bytecode-vm-interpret,\n225\tjni-reflection-callback, kotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines, dex-bytecode-integrity-gate, module-contract-member-eval,\n226\tpayload-digest-pinned-select, payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap, multi-stage-loader-recurse, classloader-shadow-resolve,\n227\tcdex-vdex-string-pool, native-payload-system-load, attestation-jws-claims, xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack.\n228\tPending retry: puzzle-entry-pointer-follow (attempt 1 failed only on an unrelated script-lane fixture timing test).\n229\t\n230\t```json\n231\t[\n232\t  {\"id\": \"anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path\", \"concept\": \"anti-debug STATE MACHINE whose clean terminal state emits the answer (D21 prompt; rows 41, 79, 89)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 named 'a clean-room anti-debug state machine ... retaining the intended app flow' and the TT dex added `debuggerGate`, but no code shipped yet. Build `anti_debug_state_scan(apk)`: find methods with a state variable (int local/field, enum ordinal, String state) reassigned inside a loop or across a packed/sparse-switch, where at least one transition depends on a probe that clean_device_scan stubs (Debug.isDebuggerConnected/waitingForDebugger, ApplicationInfo.flags & 2, TracerPid, timing deltas, Settings ADB_ENABLED). Run flattened_cfg_scan's evaluator with the clean_device probe table in the same run (one combined env), starting from the initial state set in <init>/<clinit>/onCreate, until a terminal state (loop exit / return / value appended before `proof=`). Report each terminal value with its state path; rank the clean path first and DEMOTE values reached only when a probe says 'debugged' (decoy/trap/honeypot). Budget <0.8 s, never raise.\"},\n233\t  {\"id\": \"timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs\", \"concept\": \"timing anti-debug + debug-flag probes not yet stubbed by clean_device_scan (rows 41, 50, 88)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"clean_device_scan (built) answers Build/su/frida/TracerPid/isDebuggerConnected/ApplicationInfo.flags, but not clocks or debug settings. Extend its probe table (or add a sibling pass reusing _ENV_*): SystemClock.elapsedRealtime/uptimeMillis/elapsedRealtimeNanos, System.nanoTime/currentTimeMillis, Debug.threadCpuTimeNanos -> a monotonic counter advancing by a small fixed step (1 ms / 1e6 ns) per call so 'delta < threshold' passes; Settings.Global/Secure.getInt(ADB_ENABLED|DEVELOPMENT_SETTINGS_ENABLED|adb_enabled, def) -> 0; SystemProperties/System.getProperty('ro.debuggable'|'ro.secure'|'service.adb.root') -> '0'/'1'/'0'; BuildConfig.DEBUG static -> read its encoded static value but ALSO report the release (false) path; Debug.isDebuggerConnected on android.os.Debug and VMDebug.isDebuggingEnabled -> false; Thread.sleep no-op. Test with a synthetic dex where the answer xor key depends on the delta check.\"},\n234\t  {\"id\": \"hook-framework-introspection-stubs\", \"concept\": \"Frida/Xposed/Substrate detection via stack traces, thread names, native-method flags (row 91)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Likely next resilience theme after anti-debug. Stub for the Dalvik evaluator: Thread.currentThread().getStackTrace()/new Throwable().getStackTrace() -> a short clean array (dalvik.system.VMStack, java.lang.Thread, the app's own frames from the call chain; no de.robv.android.xposed.XposedBridge, com.saurik.substrate); Thread.getAllStackTraces keys with names 'main','FinalizerDaemon' (no 'gum-js-loop','gmain','pool-frida'); File('/proc/self/task').listFiles + comm reads -> clean names; Modifier.isNative(Method.getModifiers()) on app methods -> false; ClassLoader.loadClass/Class.forName of hook classes -> ClassNotFoundException into the method's handler; /proc/self/fd readlink -> no 'linjector'/'frida-pipe'; System.getenv('CLASSPATH'/'LD_PRELOAD') -> null. Feed into clean_device_scan's run set; same ranking (clean path first).\"},\n235\t  {\"id\": \"enum-switchmap-state-resolve\", \"concept\": \"enum/sealed state machines compiled to `$SwitchMap$` / Kotlin `$WhenMappings` (row 89)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"javac compiles `switch(enumValue)` to a synthetic class `<Outer>$1` with static int[] `$SwitchMap$<pkg>$<Enum>` filled in <clinit> by `sget-object Enum.X; invoke-virtual ordinal(); const/4 k; aput` (each under a NoSuchFieldError catch); kotlinc emits `<Outer>$WhenMappings` with `$EnumSwitchMapping$0`. The Dalvik evaluator must (1) run the enum's <clinit> (new-instance Enum(name, ordinal) + values array), (2) run the switch-map <clinit>, (3) resolve `aget` of the map by ordinal before the packed-switch. Pure python over androguard or own dex parser; expose `switchmap_table(apk)` and make dalvik-mini-interpreter / flattened_cfg_scan / anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path use it. Also handle String-switch (hashCode sparse-switch + equals) already in dispatch-key-resolve.\"},\n236\t  {\"id\": \"native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate\", \"concept\": \"native anti-debug inside the `.so` (ptrace TRACEME, /proc/self/status TracerPid, prctl, fork watchdog) during unicorn emulation (row 66)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If D21's theme returns natively (JNI export gated by a native anti-debug probe), native_so_emulate_export / native_gate_branch_scan must survive libc calls. Add PLT/import stubs for the unicorn runner: ptrace -> 0 (first TRACEME succeeds), getppid -> zygote pid, prctl -> 0, fork -> -1 or child-never-runs, open/fopen/openat of /proc/self/status|/proc/<pid>/status -> a fake FILE yielding 'TracerPid:\\\\t0', fgets/read/fscanf/strstr/strncmp/atoi over it, /proc/self/maps without frida/xposed lines, access/stat on su/frida paths -> -1 ENOENT, kill/raise/abort/exit -> stop emulation as 'trap path', time/clock_gettime/gettimeofday -> monotonic small step, pthread_create -> run the start routine inline once or skip. Resolve imports via pyelftools .rela.plt; x86_64 first, arm64 via multi-abi path. Report the export's return string/byte buffer on the clean path.\"},\n237\t  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n238\t  {\"id\": \"puzzle-entry-pointer-follow\", \"concept\": \"puzzle `data` names a zip entry (D20 codec `dynamic`, row 42)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20's generic answer() returned nothing because puzzle_candidates yields `data` verbatim (`assets/payload.dex`); only the raw_entry_scan fallback saved it. Make it first-class in lib.android: when any puzzle field (data/path/module/entry/payload/file, or any string value) equals or ends with an existing zip entry name (also with `assets/` prefix added/stripped, `file:///android_asset/` stripped), read that entry and run the full candidate chain on its bytes (dex string pool incl. multi-dex, nested zip/jar/apk via nested-container-recurse, ELF strings, magic unwrap), depth <= 3, cycle-safe. Return those candidates FIRST, and never return the pointer string itself as a candidate. Also accept host-dex strings shaped `<entry>:<dotted.Class>` as pointers. D21 went back to an in-JSON codec, so this is a Mastery-mix safeguard (the d20 set recurs), not the next escalation; the 2026-10-20 attempt failed only on tests/test_lane_fixtures.py timing for a script fixture -- rerun.\"},\n239\t  {\"id\": \"exception-driven-control-flow\", \"concept\": \"probe throws, catch handler selects the path (row 90)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Anti-debug/anti-tamper code often uses try/catch as control flow (throw custom SecurityException when a probe trips; handler sets state or picks a decoy). Make the Dalvik evaluator model dex try_item/encoded_catch_handler tables fully: `throw` vX transfers to the first handler whose type is a supertype (walk the in-dex class hierarchy + a small java.lang exception tree), `move-exception` binds it, catch-all handlers, nested tries, and exceptions thrown by stubbed APIs (NameNotFound, ClassNotFound, FileNotFound, NumberFormat, ArithmeticException on div-int by zero, ArrayIndexOutOfBounds, NullPointerException on a null receiver). Verify with synthetic dexes where the ANS- value is only produced in a handler and where a decoy sits in the handler of a debugged-path throw.\"},\n240\t  {\"id\": \"emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs\", \"concept\": \"emulator detection beyond Build fields: telephony, sensors, battery, qemu pipes (row 48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend the clean-device probe table with retail-phone answers: TelephonyManager.getDeviceId/getImei/getSubscriberId/getLine1Number/getNetworkOperatorName/getSimOperatorName/getPhoneType/getSimState (non-zero IMEI-shaped, 'T-Mobile', PHONE_TYPE_GSM, SIM_STATE_READY), SensorManager.getSensorList(TYPE_ALL) -> 20+ entries with vendor names (not 'Goldfish'), getDefaultSensor -> non-null, BatteryManager/ACTION_BATTERY_CHANGED -> level 63, temperature 285, not always charging; File.exists on /dev/qemu_pipe, /dev/socket/qemud, /system/lib/libc_malloc_debug_qemu.so, /sys/qemu_trace, /dev/goldfish_pipe -> false; /proc/cpuinfo without 'Goldfish'/'hypervisor'; Build.HARDWARE/BOARD/BOOTLOADER/HOST/SERIAL real-device values; NetworkInterface without 10.0.2.15/eth0-only. Same scan integration as clean_device_scan.\"},\n241\t  {\"id\": \"biometric-auth-callback-eval\", \"concept\": \"MASVS-AUTH biometric / local auth bypass: the success callback holds the secret (row 92)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Untouched MASVS group. Find classes extending androidx.biometric.BiometricPrompt$AuthenticationCallback, android.hardware.biometrics.BiometricPrompt$AuthenticationCallback or FingerprintManager(Compat)$AuthenticationCallback, KeyguardManager.createConfirmDeviceCredentialIntent + onActivityResult(RESULT_OK). Evaluate onAuthenticationSucceeded(result) with a result whose getCryptoObject() returns null (event-bound bypass) AND with a CryptoObject wrapping a stub Cipher (doFinal = identity) -- report both values labelled; evaluate onActivityResult with resultCode -1. Also flag `setUserAuthenticationRequired(false)` / missing `setInvalidatedByBiometricEnrollment`. ANS- regex on the results; demote values reached only on onAuthenticationFailed/onAuthenticationError.\"},\n242\t  {\"id\": \"binder-ontransact-code-map\", \"concept\": \"bound Service / AIDL / Messenger: transaction code -> reply value (row 2)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Still-unused IPC surface. For every exported <service> (manifest_facts) find its Binder: classes extending android.os.Binder or `I*$Stub` overriding onTransact(int code, Parcel data, Parcel reply, int flags), and Handler subclasses used by Messenger (handleMessage(Message) switching on msg.what). Evaluate per case of the packed/sparse-switch on code/what (incl. FIRST_CALL_TRANSACTION = 1 offsets and the interface descriptor `enforceInterface` string) with a stub Parcel (readString/readInt return the constants the case compares against when solvable), collecting reply.writeString / Bundle.putString / Message.obtain(..., obj) values. Report code -> value; ANS- regex; prefer the code named in strings/manifest/meta-data.\"},\n243\t  {\"id\": \"broadcast-receiver-action-map\", \"concept\": \"exported / dynamic broadcast receiver: (action, extras) -> emitted value (row 3)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Find <receiver> components (exported, intent-filter actions, permission) and dynamic registerReceiver(IntentFilter(action)) calls; evaluate onReceive(Context, Intent) per declared action with a stub Intent whose getAction returns that action and getStringExtra/getIntExtra return the constant the code compares against (solve simple equals/== guards from const-strings in the same method), collecting setResultData/setResultExtras/Log/sendBroadcast extras/SharedPreferences.putString values. Handles ordered broadcasts (getResultData chaining). Output action -> value; ANS- regex.\"},\n244\t  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n245\t  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n246\t  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n247\t  {\"id\": \"dart-snapshot-string-pool\", \"concept\": \"Flutter release `libapp.so`: strings in the Dart AOT snapshot (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"blutter is missing and arm64-only. Pure python minimum: locate `_kDartVmSnapshotData`/`_kDartIsolateSnapshotData` via pyelftools dynsym in libapp.so, read the snapshot header (magic 0xf5f5dcdc, version hash -> Dart version), and scan the isolate data for OneByteString/TwoByteString objects (tagged length smi + bytes) plus a raw fallback (printable runs >= 6, UTF-16LE runs). Report ANS- hits and strings near `ANS`-prefixed fragments for concatenation. Also check assets/flutter_assets/kernel_blob.bin (debug builds: plain source).\"},\n248\t  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"},\n249\t  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n250\t  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n251\t  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n252\t  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n253\t  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"}\n254\t]\n255\t```"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54e61971-bfdb-459b-a2c1-7e7f4c8debc4","uuid":"4eabb1d0-d827-459b-a0ec-40967fdc71a8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:10:24.361Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/mobile-android.md","content":"the ENTRY PATH `assets/payload.dex` -- the FIRST day the answer left the JSON value: a plain `ANS-` const in payload class\n`com.huntress.arena.payload.Module` (strings `ANSWER`, `CONTRACT`, `DAY20-SIGNED-MODULE:..`). No ClassLoader/verify code\nin any host dex; TT/Mastery host dex added `moduleContract` + `assets/payload.dex:com.huntress.arena.payload.Module`.\nD21 (Debug Me If You Can, `anti_debug` \"anti-debug state checks\"; prompt \"Neutralize a clean-room anti-debug state machine\nwhile retaining the intended app flow\"): plain 6-entry fixture, codec back to `reverse` (d2/d8) -- the D20 pointer did\nNOT persist. First manifest with `android:debuggable=\"true\"` (single/TT/Mastery-d21 only). No debugger/TracerPid/clock\nAPI and no state loop in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `debuggerGate` + `STRUCTURAL`.\nSo \"seen Dn\" below means the THEME was named that day. It does NOT mean an exploit was ever needed.\nThe risk for D22+ is the **answer moving away from the JSON** (D20: one hop, D21: back in the JSON) more than the theme.\nD15-D21 read as a MASVS-RESILIENCE / obfuscation arc (native secret -> JNI gate -> name obfuscation + decoys -> string\nencryption -> reflection -> dynamic code loading -> anti-debug). Still unnamed in that arc: root, emulator, hook\n(Frida/Xposed) and tamper/repackaging checks, then obfuscation capstones (flattening, VM). After it the untouched MASVS\ngroups are AUTH (biometric/local auth) and the leftover IPC surfaces (bound Service/AIDL, broadcast receivers).\nNext expect also: the payload ENCRYPTED/wrapped (key in host dex, unwrap by\nmagic known plaintext), \"challenge-signed\" made real (several payloads, only the one whose digest/signature matches a\npinned value is loaded), >1 `ANS-` in the payload with the host-named member (`moduleContract`) deciding, class shadowing\nbetween host and payload loaders, multi-stage loaders, anti-tamper / root / emulator / debugger / Frida checks, and\ncontrol-flow flattening or a tiny VM. New codecs keep arriving (d7 caesar, d15 native, d17 indexed, d19 reflection, d20\ndynamic) and old ones recur (d18 xor, d21 reverse): check `data` for `ANS-`, then for an entry name, then decode from `ANS-` alone.\n\nTool status (after `source bin/env.sh`; checked 2026-10-15). INSTALLED: jadx 1.5.6, apktool 3.0.3, aapt, aapt2,\napksigner, keytool, jarsigner, d2j-dex2jar (+ `tools/dex2jar/d2j-*.sh`: baksmali, decrypt-string, ...), droidasc,\nandroguard (CLI + py), apkInspector, rizin/rz-bin, r2/rabin2, Ghidra `analyzeHeadless`, readelf/nm/strings, hbc-decompiler/\nhbc-disassembler/hbc-file-parser (hermes-dec), ilspycmd + dotnet, webcrack, js-beautify, sqlite3, 7z, binwalk, yara,\ntshark, zlib-flate, openssl, adb (no device). py: lief, pyelftools, capstone, unicorn, pycryptodome, lz4, plistlib.\nMISSING: blutter, reFlutter, pyxamstore, Il2CppDumper/Cpp2IL, frida/frida-tools/objection, apkid, apkleaks, bundletool,\nabe (android-backup-extractor), standalone baksmali/smali, dexdump, zipalign, de4dot, ipsw/plistutil/class-dump.\nTimed constraint: `solve.py` may use only stdlib + lib.* + pyzipper/pyelftools/pefile/capstone/pycryptodome/androguard,\nno subprocess, <1 s per set. Prebuilt extractors must be pure python.\n\n## Concept table\n\nLegend: tool `[i]` = installed here, `[M]` = missing. \"puzzle\" = `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (`lib.android.puzzle_candidates`).\n\n| # | concept | status | where the answer likely hides | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D22+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Exported Activity / implicit-export default | seen D1 | puzzle; real CTFs: `onCreate` reveals the flag when started with a magic extra | `android:exported=\"true\"`, intent-filter w/o `exported` + targetSdk<31 | `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml` [i]; `droidasc getmanifest x.apk` [i]; `lib.android.manifest_facts` | high: Mastery mixes old days |\n| 2