/res/raw/META-INF/puzzle JSON base64 fields; `-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE`, 30 82 DER), parse with a minimal pure-python DER walker (no subprocess), extract the extension, decode the AuthorizationList, report all fields; ANS- regex on challenge/octet strings (also hex/ASCII of verifiedBootHash); compare attestationApplicationId signature digest to signing_certs(apk) and verifiedBootState to the dex constants the app compares. Clean = Verified + deviceLocked true.\"},\n {\"id\":\"installer-source-and-tamper-probe-stubs\",\"concept\":\"anti-tamper / repackaging probes: installer source, signature, debuggable flag, dex CRC (rows 49, 50)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"After root/emulator/hook the arc names tamper checks. Extend the clean-device probe table: PackageManager.getInstallerPackageName / getInstallSourceInfo().getInstallingPackageName / getInitiatingPackageName -> 'com.android.vending'; getPackageInfo(own, GET_SIGNATURES|GET_SIGNING_CERTIFICATES).signatures/signingInfo.getApkContentsSigners -> the APK's REAL v1/v2 cert bytes from signing_certs(apk) (so hashCode/MessageDigest comparisons evaluate on the true digest); ApplicationInfo.flags FLAG_DEBUGGABLE bit from the manifest; ApplicationInfo.sourceDir/publicSourceDir -> '/data/app/<pkg>-1/base.apk'; ZipFile(sourceDir).getEntry('classes.dex').getCrc() -> the real CRC from the APK; Context.getPackageCodePath likewise. Integrate with dex_integrity_gate_scan / integrity_key_scan (built) so a digest-keyed answer uses real bytes. Report the value on the untampered path.\"},\n {\"id\":\"native-system-property-and-mounts-stubs\",\"concept\":\"native root/emulator probes via __system_property_get, popen and /proc/self/mounts inside the .so (rows 66, 95)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate (built) covers ptrace/TracerPid/access/stat. Add unicorn import stubs: __system_property_get(name, buf) / __system_property_find + __system_property_read(_callback) -> clean values (ro.build.tags release-keys, ro.debuggable 0, ro.secure 1, ro.boot.verifiedbootstate green, ro.boot.flash.locked 1, ro.kernel.qemu '', ro.hardware a real SoC); popen/pclose + fgets for 'which su'/'getprop'/'mount' -> clean text; fopen('/proc/self/mounts'|'/proc/mounts'|'/proc/self/mountinfo') -> lines without magisk/tmpfs-on-/system/overlay; opendir/readdir on /data/adb, /sbin -> empty; dlopen of libmagisk/libfrida -> NULL. Same import resolution path (pyelftools .rela.plt), x86_64 then arm64.\"},\n {\"id\":\"native-inline-syscall-stubs\",\"concept\":\"native probes issuing raw syscalls (svc #0 / syscall instruction) to bypass libc hooks\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Hardened root/anti-hook checks call openat/faccessat/readlinkat/newfstatat/ptrace/getppid directly via `syscall` (x86_64) or `svc #0` (arm64) so Frida libc hooks miss them. In the unicorn runner, hook UC_HOOK_INSN syscall (x86_64) / UC_HOOK_INTR (arm64), dispatch on rax/x8 number (x86_64: openat 257, faccessat 269, newfstatat 262, readlinkat 267, read 0, close 3, ptrace 101, getppid 110; arm64: openat 56, faccessat 48, newfstatat 79, readlinkat 78, read 63, close 57, ptrace 117, getppid 173) and answer from the same clean filesystem/proc model as the libc stubs (ENOENT for su paths, fake fd for /proc/self/status with TracerPid 0). Test with a tiny hand-assembled .so.\"},\n {\"id\":\"play-integrity-verdict-select\",\"concept\":\"Play Integrity / SafetyNet verdict JSON drives the branch: pick the value for the strongest clean verdict (row 87)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"attestation-jws-claims (built) decodes tokens. Add verdict semantics: parse decoded payloads or plain JSON assets with requestDetails{requestPackageName, nonce, timestampMillis}, appIntegrity{appRecognitionVerdict PLAY_RECOGNIZED|UNRECOGNIZED_VERSION|UNEVALUATED, packageName, certificateSha256Digest[], versionCode}, deviceIntegrity{deviceRecognitionVerdict [MEETS_BASIC_INTEGRITY, MEETS_DEVICE_INTEGRITY, MEETS_STRONG_INTEGRITY, MEETS_VIRTUAL_INTEGRITY]}, accountDetails{appLicensingVerdict LICENSED}, legacy SafetyNet ctsProfileMatch/basicIntegrity/evaluationType HARDWARE_BACKED. When several verdict blobs or dex branches exist, rank the one with PLAY_RECOGNIZED + MEETS_DEVICE/STRONG_INTEGRITY + LICENSED + certificateSha256Digest equal to signing_certs(apk) + nonce matching the host's computed nonce; report the ANS- value tied to it; demote others as decoys.\"},\n {\"id\":\"whitebox-table-cipher-eval\",\"concept\":\"white-box / table-driven cipher (lookup-table AES or byte S-box chains) as an obfuscation capstone\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"After VM/flattening the next obfuscation step is table-based crypto with the key folded into large static arrays (int[256]/byte[4096] T-boxes, Tyi tables, or chained byte S-boxes) in dex <clinit> or .so .rodata. Don't recover the key: evaluate the table walk. Dex: dex_array_scan to pull the arrays, then run the decrypt method in the Dalvik evaluator with arrays preloaded (raise its step budget for 10-16 rounds of aget/xor); .so: unicorn-run the export over .rodata tables. Fallback: if the method is a pure byte-wise S-box chain, compose the tables in python and invert via the ANS- known plaintext. Budget <0.8 s.\"},\n]\nfor g in new:\n    assert g['id'] not in keep_by and ('mobile-android:'+g['id']) not in st, g['id']\npending=[g for g in keep if g['action']=='prebuild']\n# order: P1 new, P1 kept, P2 new, P2 kept prebuild, others\nallg=new+keep\norder=sorted(range(len(allg)),key=lambda i:(allg[i]['priority'],0 if allg[i]['action']=='prebuild' else 1,i))\nallg=[allg[i] for i in order]\nfor g in allg: assert set(g)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'}\npending_n=sum(1 for g in allg if g['action']=='prebuild' and not done(g['id']))\nprint('pending prebuild',pending_n,[g['id'] for g in allg])\nbody=\"\"\"## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\n\"\"\"+ \", \".join(built) + \"\"\".\nForecast after D22: the arc is walking MASVS-RESILIENCE one control per day (D21 anti-debug, D22 root). Next most likely:\nemulator detection, hook/Frida detection, tamper/installer/signature checks, attestation (key attestation `RootOfTrust`,\nPlay Integrity), then obfuscation capstones. Code-side gates have never shipped (TT dex only names the mechanic:\n`debuggerGate`, `rootSignals`); the gaps below harden the clean-device evaluator for the day one does.\n\n```json\n\"\"\" + \"[\\n\" + \",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in allg) + \"\\n]\\n```\\n\"\nopen(p,'w').write(head+body)\nPYEOF\n.venv/bin/python -I $TMPDIR/gaps.py && python3 -c \"\nimport re,json;s=open('reference/coverage/mobile-android.md').read();j=json.loads(re.search(r'\\`\\`\\`json\\n(.*?)\\n\\`\\`\\`',s,re.S).group(1));print(len(j))\"; wc -l reference/coverage/mobile-android.md"}}}
